Just so everybody knows, jbovlaste is now up to version 0.7

As far as I can tell, 0.7 is data-complete, meaning that the databse is
currently storing everything that the database is likely to be asked to
store.

There is still a fair bit to do in terms of the user interface, but all
the basic functionality is there.

Therefore:

    I will not be wiping the jbovlaste databse again if I can possibly
    help it.

I honestly have no idea what could be needed to added to the databse at
this poing that wouldn't be completely backwards compatible.  In fact, I
have no idea what the database needs beyond what it has right now.

So:

    Please begin entering real words into jbovlaste if you can stand the
    user interface.  I will make every effort to ensure that your data
    is not removed in the future, ever.

This includes instituting backups.

-Robin

